# CMS69 BMI Screening Cognitive Support — caseload

// Scenario: a patient eligible for BMI screening has a documented high
// BMI and an overweight diagnosis on file. The CMS69 BMI Screening
// Strategy decision walks the high-BMI branch and the Recommend High
// BMI Intervention sub-decision chooses the weight-assessment-referral
// path.
//
// This case exercises the decision-tree path:
//   CMS69 BMI Screening Strategy
//     when Patient Eligible For BMI Screening
//       when Has Documented High BMI
//         use decision Recommend High BMI Intervention
//           when Patient Has Overweight or Obese Diagnosis
//             any: recommend Order Weight Assessment Referral

library "CMS69 BMI Cognitive Support — High BMI".
covers "CMS69 BMI Screening GPG Strategy example".


// ============ Patient facts ============

fact "Jane Doe":
- name is "Jane Doe".
- birth date is "1980-01-01".
- defined by "Patient".


// ============ Clinical facts ============

fact "Wellness Visit":
- code is "99395".
- date is "2026-01-15".
- defined by "Encounter".

fact "Documented High BMI":
- code is "39156-5".
- date is "2026-01-15".
- value is 32.4.
- defined by "CMS69 BMI Screening GPG Strategy example"."BMI as an Observation".

fact "Overweight Diagnosis":
- code is "E66.3".
- date is "2024-09-08".
- defined by "CMS69 BMI Screening GPG Strategy example"."Overweight or Obese Diagnoses".


// ============ Cases ============

case "Jane: documented high BMI triggers weight-assessment-referral recommendation":
- description is `Jane is eligible for BMI screening, has a recently-
  documented high BMI, and an existing overweight diagnosis on file.
  The Recommend High BMI Intervention sub-decision selects the
  weight-assessment-referral branch.`.
- subject is "Jane Doe".
- fact is "Wellness Visit".
- fact is "Documented High BMI".
- fact is "Overweight Diagnosis".
- result is "CMS69 BMI Screening Strategy" is "Order Weight Assessment Referral".
